+The two coefficients `a(t),b(t)` have common displayed denominator
+`q^3 Q2(t) P4(t)^3`.  Before cancellation, the complete new scalar list is
+`t`, `t-(t-1)=1`, and the Euler factors
+`4t+1,2t+3,5,7-2t`, together with `2,3,q,t+1,3t+2` and the already audited
+`y,p_C(t,t-1),p_Q(t,2t-2)`.  The last Euler numerator `f_3` is zero, so its
+division is avoidable; the executable nevertheless performs it, and
+`7-2t!=0` for every integer `t>=5`.  The primitive new pivot-norm factors are
+`P4(t)` and `Q2(t)`.  Thus every denominator in (6.2)--(6.3) is positive for
+`t>=5` except the explicitly negative but nonzero `7-2t`, and every numerator
+factor in (6.2) is positive.
+Consequently `lambda_(t,t-1)` is a unit of `A_t` for every integer `t>=5`,
+including both factors of every split algebra.  Exact coefficient-pair runs
+at `t=5,...,15` agree with (6.2).  Direct authenticated rows give, for stored
