+## 6. A uniform outer-axis factorization
+
+The same grading gives a useful additional check.  On the coordinate axis
+`b3=b4=u_2=...=u_(t-2)=0`, put `z=u_(t-1)`,
+`s=z/X^(t-1)` and `Delta_n=n-(t-1)Theta`.  For `t>=5`, the only high
