+For the denominator audit, the new scalars before cancellation are
+
+```text
+t, c=t-j, 2c+1=q-2j,
+4t+1, 2t+2c+1, 4c+1, 6c-2t+1,                       (6.7)
+```
+
+together with `2,3,q,t+1,3t+2,y,p_C(t,j),p_Q(t,2j)` already covered in
+Section 2.  The last Euler numerator `f_3` is zero, so the last division is
